Revisions of OPCD_2.0 to obtain OPCD_2.1
****************************************

19.02.05. Contents of OPCD_update_2.1

Revised codes opfit.f and accfit.f.
***********************************
The codes interpolate to a mesh in (R,T) (R=RHO/T_6^3)
For given R interpolations in T require at least 
5 tabulated T values. In some exceptional circumstances
that condition is not satisfied and a run will fail.
The modification of 06.01.05 changes, if necessary,
the mesh in (R ,T) such that the condition is satisfied.

The codes opfit.f.gz and accfit.f.gz in OPCD_update_2.1 should 
replace the corresponding codes in OPCD_2.0/codes.

The new code accfitP.f.
***********************
The original code accfit.f reads a file acc.zz created
by accv.f containing vales of GAMMA on the (T,Ne) mesh 
points. The code accfit.f interpolates to values of
(T,RHO) for a stellar model and gives output of LOG10(GAMMA)
and LOG10(g_rad). If GAMMA is negative it prints a message
and sets LOG10(GAMMA) and LOG10(g_rad) equal to 1.E-30. 
The new code, accfitP.f, gives output values of GAMMA and 
g_rad (NOT LOG10). It is to be preferred if negative values 
GAMMA occur on the (T,RHO) mesh.
Input to accfitP.f is the same as that to accfit.f

The code accfitP.f.gz should be added to the codes in OPCD_2.0/codes.
  
The new code accvff.f.
***********************
The original code accv.f calculates data for radiative 
accelerations allowing for momentum-transfer-to-electrons
(mte corrections) for bound-free (bf) processes but not for
free-free (ff). The new code accvff.f includes allowance for
mte for ff. It uses the theory of
K. El-Murr and G. Massacrier, J. Phys. B, 31, 4303, 1998
and of K. El-Murr, Thesis, Lyon, 1999.
Input to accvff.f is the same as that to accv.f
The importance of mte for ff processes is discussed by
M.J. Seaton, "Updated radiative accelerations from the 
Opacity Project", to be submitted MNRAS.
In most cases inclusion of mte for ff does not produce
important changes in g_rad, but there are some exceptional
cases. Negative values of GAMMA are more likely to occur
with accvff.f and when they do occur it will be advisable
to process the output from accvff.f using  accfitP.f rather 
than accfit.f.

The code accvff.f.gz should be added to the codes in OPCD_2.0/codes.

The new makefile and BASHOP
***************************
The makefile and BASHOP in OPCD_update_2.1 should 
replace the corresponding files in OPCD_2.0. To recompile codes
just type "make" or "./BASHOP". Note: BASHOP will also reinstall
the data files and proceed with tests, and will not work if the
data formatted files have been erased with procedures CLEANOP or
"make clean".
Finally, the directory OPCD_2.0 should be renamed OPCD_2.1
